{"orgCode":"4560","name":"Behavioral Health Services Oversight and Accountability Commission","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"The Commission's goal is to provide oversight and accountability for portions of the Behavioral Health Services Act. The Commission works in partnership to promote access to effective and culturally competent support for individuals living with behavioral health conditions and their families.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":66559,"cy":78251,"by":71440},"positions":{"py":53.6,"cy":56,"by":56}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/4560","kind":"department","name":"Behavioral Health Services Oversight and Accountability Commission","code":"4560","amounts":{"py":66559,"cy":78251,"by":71440},"positions":{"py":53.6,"cy":56,"by":56},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":66559,"cy":78251,"by":71440}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4560/4170","kind":"program","name":"Behavioral Health Services Oversight and Accountability Commission","code":"4170","amounts":{"py":66559,"cy":78251,"by":71440},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":66559,"cy":78251,"by":71440}},"positions":{"py":53.6,"cy":56,"by":56},"description":"4170 -\nBehavioral Health Services Oversight and Accountability Commission\n\nThe Commission, established in 2004 and updated in 2025 under the Behavioral Health Services Act (BHSA), provides BHSA oversight and accountability through research and evaluation, grants, technical assistance, and community engagement.\n\nResearch and Evaluation\n\nThe Commission conducts research and program evaluations of BHSA initiatives and publishes high-level county and state-wide data.\n\nGrants\n\nThe Commission manages grant programs that incentivize stronger partnerships, integrated services, and evaluation of BHSA initiatives. The Commission's grant programs include the Mental Health Wellness Act, the Behavioral Health Student Services Act, early intervention grants which include allcove youth drop-in centers and early psychosis intervention programs, and the Innovation Partnership Fund.\n\nPolicy Projects\n\nThe Commission may advise the Governor and the Legislature regarding actions the state may take to improve care and services for individuals living with behavioral health conditions. The Commission executes projects designed to inform behavioral health policy by integrating research findings and experiential knowledge. The Commission's projects include criminal justice mental health, the state suicide prevention plan, workplace mental health standards, prevention and early intervention strategies, and school-based mental health.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":21433,"cy":36744,"by":17134},"Local Assistance":{"py":45126,"cy":41507,"by":54306}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4560/4170/f3085","kind":"fund","name":"Behavioral Health Services Fund","code":"3085","amounts":{"py":66559,"cy":78251,"by":51440},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":66559,"cy":78251,"by":51440}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":21433,"cy":36744,"by":17134},"Local Assistance":{"py":45126,"cy":41507,"by":34306}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/4560/4170/f3485","kind":"fund","name":"Behavioral Health Services Act Innovation Partnership Fund","code":"3485","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":20000},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":20000}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":20000}}}}]}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/4560","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/4560"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/4000/4560.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"Welfare and Institutions Code, Division 5, Part 3, Part 3.1, Part 3.2, Part 3.4, Part 3.6, Part 3.7, Part 3.8, Part 4, and Part 4.5."}},"funding":{"id":"exp/4000/4560/funding","kind":"root","name":"Behavioral Health Services Oversight and Ac